  <!-- Privacy Policy Content -->
  <div class="legal-content container">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="effective-date">Effective date: August 1, 2026</p>

    <h2>About This Policy</h2>
    <p>This policy explains how Cadenza Studio collects, uses, and protects information when teachers, studios, families, and students use the application.</p>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>We collect information used to create and manage accounts and studio relationships. This may include names, email addresses, phone numbers, login and security information, studio details, teacher profiles, family relationships, student names, age or age band, instruments, experience level, goals, and preferences.</p>
    <p>When you use Cadenza Studio, we also store information you and other members of your studio add to the service. This may include lesson schedules and attendance, messages, lesson notes, assignments, practice logs, shared resources, and files. We also receive technical information needed to operate and protect the service, such as device or browser details, IP address, and request logs.</p>

    <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
    <p>We use information to provide and maintain Cadenza Studio, authenticate users, connect teachers, families, and students, deliver features, send notifications, provide support, and improve the service. We may also use information to meet legal obligations and enforce our terms.</p>

    <h2>Data Storage and Sharing</h2>
    <p>Cadenza Studio is designed to run locally. Your studio data stays on your own machine unless you choose a hosted deployment. Information is not shared with third parties for advertising or analytics purposes. Data is only accessible to you, the authorized administrators of your studio, and the families and students you connect.</p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>We use standard security practices to protect information, including encrypted connections and access controls. No system can guarantee complete security, so please use a strong, unique password and contact us if you suspect unauthorized access.</p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>We keep information for as long as needed to provide Cadenza Studio and maintain your studio records. You may request deletion of your data at any time.</p>

    <h2>Access, Correction, and Deletion</h2>
    <p>You can update your account and profile information within Cadenza Studio. You may also ask us to access, correct, or delete your personal information by contacting us.</p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy as Cadenza Studio changes. We will post the updated policy here and change the effective date.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions or requests, contact us through our <a href="/cadenza/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
  </div>

